.TH OXTERM 1 "2026-10-26" "oxterm 1.1.18" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oxterm \- GTK3/VTE terminal emulator with notes, history and remote sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oxterm
.RI [ DIRECTORY ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR CMD ...]
.br
.B oxterm
.BR \-a | \-M
.RI [ SESSION_ID ]
.br
.B oxterm
.B \-\-detach
.I SESSION_ID
.br
.B oxterm
.B \-\-list
.br
.BI oxterm " {new|split|send|capture|wait} [OPTIONS]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oxterm
is a terminal emulator for Linux built on GTK3 and VTE. It provides tabs,
splits, command history, Markdown notes, shell integration, profiles and
persistent PTY sessions that can be attached to over SSH.
.PP
With no arguments a window is opened and the configured shell is started in
.IR DIRECTORY ,
the working directory of the caller, or the directory restored from the last
session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-working\-directory " " DIR
Working directory for the new terminal.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-title " " TITLE
Set a fixed window title that applications cannot override.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-geometry " " COLSxROWS
Initial size in character cells, for example
.BR 120x40 .
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-maximize
Start maximized.
.TP
.BR \-\-class " " CLASS
Set the class part of the WM_CLASS property.
.TP
.BR \-\-name " " NAME
Set the instance part of the WM_CLASS property.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " " NAME
Start with a saved profile. The selection lasts for this session only.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " FILE
Use an alternative settings file instead of
.IR ~/.config/oxterm/settings.json .
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-option " " KEY=VALUE
Override a setting for this session. May be repeated. Values are not written
back to the settings file.
.TP
.BR \-\-font " " FAMILY
Override the font family for this session.
.TP
.BR \-\-font\-size " " N
Override the font size for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new window instead of reusing a running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-restore
Do not restore the last session.
.TP
.B \-\-hold
Keep the terminal open after the command exits.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-execute " " CMD ...
Run a command instead of the configured shell. All remaining arguments are
passed to the command.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat the next argument as a directory even if it starts with a dash.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List active Oxterm terminals. The first column is the session ID used by
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-M ,
.B \-\-info
and
.BR \-\-detach .
.TP
.BR \-\-info " " SESSION_ID
Show details about one active terminal.
.TP
.BR \-\-broker " " SOCKET " " ID
Internal entry point that runs the persistent PTY broker. Not meant to be
called directly.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version, including the build commit count as SemVer build metadata
(for example
.BR 1.1.11+116 ),
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the command line summary and exit.
.SH CONTROL API
These subcommands act on a running Oxterm window on the same host and open no
window, so they are safe to use over SSH. Each prints its result on standard
output. A target pane can be given with
.BR \-\-pane ;
otherwise Oxterm uses
.BR OXTERM_PANE ,
then the only open pane.
.TP
.B oxterm new
.RI [ DIRECTORY ]
.RI [ \-\-cwd " " DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-title " " TITLE ]
.RI [ "\-\- " COMMAND " ...]"
Open a new tab, run
.I COMMAND
there when given, and print the new pane id.
.I DIRECTORY
is a shorthand for
.BR \-\-cwd .
.TP
.B oxterm split
.RI [ \-\-pane " " ID ]
.RB [ \-\-vertical | \-\-horizontal ]
.RI [ \-\-cwd " " DIR ]
.RI [ \-\-title " " TITLE ]
.RI [ "\-\- " COMMAND " ...]"
Split the target pane's window, which must still have a single pane, and print
the new pane id. The default is a vertical split.
.TP
.B oxterm send
.RI [ \-\-pane " " ID ]
.RI [ \-\-enter ]
.I TEXT ...
.br
.B oxterm send
.RI [ \-\-pane " " ID ]
.RI [ \-\-enter ]
.B \-
Type
.I TEXT
into the target pane, or standard input with
.BR \- .
With
.B \-\-enter
a carriage return is appended, as if Enter had been pressed. Read-only mode is
respected.
.TP
.B oxterm capture
.RI [ \-\-pane " " ID ]
.RB [ \-\-scrollback " " N | \-\-all ]
Print the target pane's text: the visible screen by default, the last
.I N
lines of history with
.BR \-\-scrollback ,
or the whole buffer with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.B oxterm wait
.RI [ \-\-pane " " ID ]
.RI [ \-\-timeout " " SECONDS ]
Wait for the next command in the pane to finish and exit with that command's
status, clamped to 0-255. Without
.B \-\-timeout
it waits indefinitely.
.SH REMOTE SESSIONS
These commands act on a running Oxterm terminal on the same host, open no
window and are safe to use over SSH. Without a
.IR SESSION_ID ,
.B \-a
and
.B \-M
use the only session or show a list to choose from.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attach " [" SESSION_ID "]"
Add this terminal as another view of the session and repaint its current
screen. The shell keeps running, the original window stays live, and every
view shares the same input and output.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-move " [" SESSION_ID "]"
Like
.BR \-a ,
but take control: every other remote client is disconnected and the original
window's view is switched off. In that window, Ctrl+B then
.B s
or
.B w
brings the view back.
.TP
.BR \-\-detach " " SESSION_ID
Release every remote client without stopping the shell, leaving the original
window as the only view again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oxterm/settings.json
User settings. Written by the Preferences dialog and reloaded while the
application is running.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oxterm/history.db
SQLite database with the command history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oxterm/remote/
Private directory (mode 0700) with the Unix sockets of persistent sessions and
the control socket of the running window.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/oxterm/notes/
Default directory for Markdown notes, unless
.B notes_dir
is set to another directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/oxterm/manual.md
Full user manual, including keyboard shortcuts and built-in commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Set to
.B xterm-256color
for the child process.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Set to
.B truecolor
for the child process.
.TP
.B OXTERM\_SHELL\_INTEGRATION
Set to
.B 1
for the child shell when OSC 133 shell integration is enabled in the
settings. The shell scripts use it to install their prompt and pre-exec hooks.
.TP
.B OXTERM\_SSH\_SHARING
Set to
.B 1
or
.B 0
for the child shell. The bundled SSH wrapper uses it to enable or disable
ControlMaster connection sharing.
.TP
.B OXTERM\_OSC133\_FIFO
Internal. Path of the private FIFO used by the shell integration to report
prompt events without polluting the terminal output.
.TP
.B OXTERM\_PANE
Set for every shell started by Oxterm to the pane id of that terminal, so the
control commands can address the calling pane.
.TP
.B OXTERM\_CONTROL
Set for every shell started by Oxterm to the path of the window's control
socket.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B oxterm ~/src/project
Open a terminal in a directory.
.TP
.B oxterm \-e make \-j8
Run one command in the terminal.
.TP
.B oxterm \-T build \-g 120x40
Open a terminal with a fixed title and size.
.TP
.B oxterm \-\-list
Show active sessions and their IDs.
.TP
.B ssh server oxterm \-a
Attach to a live session from another computer.
.TP
.B oxterm send \-\-pane 12345\-2 \-\-enter 'make test'
Type a command into a pane of a running window.
.TP
.B oxterm wait \-\-pane 12345\-2 \-\-timeout 600
Wait for that command and exit with its status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when an operation fails, 2 when the command line cannot be
parsed, 3 when a control command cannot find the requested pane and 4 when no
running Oxterm window can be reached.
.B oxterm wait
exits with the status of the command it observed instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR script (1)
.PP
The project page is at https://github.com/buzzqw/oxterm.
